"""
Train repeated alarm prediction model — v6 (schema-aligned).

Key changes from v5:
  C1.  Column names now exactly match the PostgreSQL alarm_data schema:
         id, time, type, status, threat_level, resolved_on, fibre_line,
         position_m, latitude, longitude, route, route_distance_m,
         marker_name, occurrence_type, record_id
       No more alias guessing — canonical names are the DB column names.

  C2.  New feature: resolution_time_hours — derived from resolved_on - time.
       Long resolution = chronic / complex alarms → stronger repeat signal.

  C3.  New feature: unresolved_share per pattern-month — ratio of alarms
       with no resolved_on value. Persistent open alarms indicate hotspots.

  C4.  New feature: status distribution — share of each status value
       (e.g., "Active", "Resolved", "Pending") as numeric ratios per bin.

  C5.  fibre_line as a categorical grouping feature (replaces FibreLine alias).
       Added to FEATURES and CATEGORICAL for OHE treatment.

  C6.  occurrence_type split improved — dedicated accident_count, alarm_count,
       and alarm_share features, now sourced from the correct column name.

  C7.  threat_level ordinal encoding preserved (Low=1, Medium=2, High/Red=3).

  C8.  record_id used only for deduplication on load (drop duplicates by PK).

  C9.  resolved_on parsed as timestamp; NaT = still open.

  C10. All column references use snake_case to match DB exactly.

  C11. Logging improved — prints actual column names found in DB on startup.

  C12. Output CSV columns updated to reflect new feature names.

Run:
    pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn joblib sqlalchemy psycopg2-binary
    python train_repeated_alarm_model_v6.py
"""

